
Developing Public and Private Entities into Federal Contractors in the United States 


    Public Entities


1. Creating the Public Entity:

LLC-1 - BizFile Online (Creates SOS File Number)

SS-4 - IRS.gov (Creates EIN) (Allow 10-15 business days after EIN issuance for IRS data to sync with SAM.gov before attempting registration.)

Statement of Information (Form LLC-12) - BizFile Online (Updates State Records. Initial filing is due within 90 days of formation; subsequent filings are due every two years. )

FinCEN BOI Reporting – FinCEN.gov: As of August 14, 2026, U.S. companies and U.S. persons are permanently exempt from BOI reporting requirements. Reporting may be required for certain foreign entities registered to do business in a U.S. state. Check FinCEN.gov for current applicability.


2. Developing the Public Entity into a Federal Contractor:

SOS + EIN - Local City Tax Bureau (Creates Municipal Business Account Number) 

Local Business License – City/County Clerk (Creates Local Business License Number)

CDTFA Online (Generates a State Seller’s Permit / Sales Tax Account Number)

Legal Name + Address + EIN - SAM.gov (Validates Entity & Assigns Federal UEI Number)

NAICS Codes + PSC Codes + Reps & Certs – SAM.gov’s SAM Wizard (Completed Prior To Profile Submission)

Immediate & Highest-Level Owner Disclosures – SAM.gov (Discloses ownership structure for compliance, if applicable)

Notarized Entity Administrator Letter – FSD.gov: Required for formal Entity Administrator designation (if auto-assignment fails or using third-party agents).

Automated DLA Push - SAM.gov (Pushes profile to DLA to generate/assign CAGE Code)

Procurement-Specific Reps & Certs – Solicitation Platform (e.g., SAM.gov, eBuy, GSA eOffer) 

Annual SAM.gov Renewal – SAM.gov (Maintains Active Registration Status)


    Private Entities


1. Creating the Private Entity:

Articles of Incorporation or Organization - WY, NM. or DE SOS Online (Creates Parent SOS File Number)

SS-4 - IRS.gov (Creates EIN) (Allow 10-15 business days after EIN issuance for IRS data to sync with SAM.gov before attempting registration.)

Annual/Biennial Corporate Report - Out-of-State Online (Updates State Records via Registered Agent)

Form 8832  (Optional) - IRS Mailing Address (Elects Non-Default Federal Tax Classification) 
(Important Note for California: If your LLC is doing business in California, the FTB imposes a minimum $800 annual franchise tax, regardless of your federal tax election. This tax is due every year, including the first year, by the 15th day of the 4th month after formation.)

FinCEN BOI Reporting – FinCEN.gov: As of August 14, 2026, U.S. companies and U.S. persons are permanently exempt from BOI reporting requirements. Reporting may be required for certain foreign entities registered to do business in a U.S. state. Check FinCEN.gov for current applicability.


2. Developing the Private Entity into a Federal Contractor:

Form LLC-1 for CA Subsidiary LLC or Form ARTS-GS for CA Subsidiary General Stock Corp – BizFile Online: Creates CA Operating Subsidiary

SS-4 - IRS.gov (Creates EIN for Subsidiary)

Statement of Information (Form LLC-12 or SI-550) - BizFile Online (Updates State Records listing the Out-of-State Parent Corporation as the Sole Member or Parent Shareholder. (Initial filing is due within 90 days of formation; subsequent filings are due every two years for LLCs.)

SOS + EIN - Local City Tax Bureau (Creates Municipal Business Account Number) 

Local Business License – City/County Clerk (Creates Local Business License Number)

CDTFA Online (Generates CA State Seller’s Permit / Sales Tax Account Number)

Legal Name + Address + EIN - SAM.gov (Creates Federal UEI Number)

NAICS Codes + PSC Codes + Reps & Certs – SAM.gov’s SAM Wizard (Completed Prior To Profile Submission)

Immediate & Highest-Level Owner Disclosures – SAM.gov (Discloses ownership structure, including Parent Corporation details, for federal compliance)

Notarized Entity Administrator Letter – FSD.gov: Required for formal Entity Administrator designation (if auto-assignment fails or using third-party agents)

Automated DLA Push - SAM.gov (Pushes profile to DLA to generate/assign CAGE Code)

Procurement-Specific Reps & Certs – Solicitation Platform (e.g., SAM.gov, eBuy, GSA eOffer) 

Set-Aside Program Applications – SBA.gov (Optional: applies for 8(a), HUBZone, WOSB, or SDVOSB certifications for competitive advantage) (Note that 8(a) requires a two-year operational history in business prior to application.)

Annual SAM.gov Renewal – SAM.gov (Maintains Active Registration Status)